  "description": "A parametric WASHING MACHINE on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE DOOR IS A CIRCLE ROW, and it is what makes the plan readable. A white rectangle in a utility room could be anything; a rectangle with a circle in it is a washing machine to everyone who has ever read a plan. render-2d's circle kind takes a centre and a radius in its third column, so the door costs one row.\n\nFRONT OR TOP LOADING swaps which piece exists: a front loader gets the circle and no lid, a top loader gets a recessed lid panel and no circle. Both keep the carcass, the control panel and every published figure.\n\nDRUM VOLUME is derived from the door radius and the depth at 55%, which is roughly what a drum occupies behind its opening — a usable estimate, and clearly an estimate rather than a measurement.",
